title: CHECKPOINT 2026-06-14 — three releases shipped; Paradigm Suite renaissance begins
summary: 'Session checkpoint / context-clear handoff. One day, three published releases from a single ''mega audit'' spree: v7.0 ''Close the Loop'' (the keystone — claimant-owned task DAG, settlement closes the learning loop, falsifiable liveness, Cid becomes a real captain), v7.1 ''fast-follows'' (CLI/Symphony loop-closure, learned token calibration, notebook open-loop fix), v7.2 ''enforcement honesty + task management for humans'' (T-005 enforcement verifies completion not invocation, the paradigm task CLI, provider-agnostic GitHub one-way sync live-tested against the real repo). Every risky call went through team analysis + adversarial review, which caught false claims (v7.0 design, v7.1 belief-delta gate) and a live sync bug (v7.2 assignee) BEFORE they shipped. NEXT ARC = the Paradigm Suite renaissance: the substrate is deep, the surfaces (Platform web, Conductor native, separate Sentinel/University UIs, VS Code ext) are fragmented — unify into one locally-launchable suite, spearheaded by the Tasks UI. See memory: project_paradigm_suite_renaissance + project_platform_tasks_section. Opening move next session: audit the surfaces first.'
